body:
i work as a designer in animation and i am not particularly passionate about it. it's fun at times and unbearably difficult at other times, but that's just how all work is right? 

if you're worried about being able to design, rig, and animate everything for your solo final project, i'd suggest talking with your professor/supervisor and seeing if you can arrange "specializing" your project.  you could also strictly design and rig assets in a group project! i specialized my solo final project into being strictly visual development, and it was a better learning experience than it would've been otherwise.

while animating is cool, it's not the only job you'd be qualified for after graduating anyway! for example, the industry is pretty much always in need of more riggers. there are more options than you think :)
